.TH VIBEOS-WEATHER 1 "2026-11-17" "vibeos 0.1.0" "VibeOS"
.SH NAME
vibeos-weather \- weather app for VibeOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vibeos-weather
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the weather where the phone is: now, the next 24 hours, today against yesterday, the week and the details.
The place is the city set with
.B Set City
in the app's menu, if one is (Open-Meteo's geocoding finds the cities as their name is typed; the city is kept in the
.B vibeos.Weather
setting
.BR city );
otherwise the first city in GNOME Weather if it has one, otherwise where GeoClue puts the phone (city accuracy),
named by OpenStreetMap's Nominatim.
.B Use my location
in Set City goes back from a set city to those. The forecast is Open-Meteo's (no key). The last place and forecast
are kept in
.I ~/.cache/vibeos-launcher/
so the app opens on them at once. The menu's
.B About
says where the data comes from and under which licences.
.SH SEE ALSO
geoclue(5)
